A new **Tormach PathPilot Lathe** post (`assets/posts/tormach-lathe.cps`). PathPilot is LinuxCNC, so Fanuc Lathe output doesn't run on a Tormach lathe (#612).

## Sources (cited in the script header and `docs/decisions/612-pathpilot-lathe-post.md`)
- [LinuxCNC G-code reference](https://linuxcnc.org/docs/html/gcode/g-code.html) and [Lathe User Information](https://linuxcnc.org/docs/html/lathe/lathe-user.html): under G7, X is a diameter but the arc's I stays a radius.
- Tormach's public 15L and 8L programming pages: the T word is tool + geometry offset; no M6; G7 only; G18 only; G20/G21 before motion; G76 I/J/K are diameter values; G30 before tool changes; no G80/G81/G83/G43.

## How each operation posts
- **Header:** `G7 G18 G20|G21 G90 G91.1 G40 G95`, then `G64 P…`. No `%` and no O word, since LinuxCNC's O is a subroutine label.
- **Tool change:** `G30`, then `T0101` (tool 1-99).
- **Spindle:** `G97 S.. M3`, or `G96 D<machine max rpm> S<surface speed> M3`.
- **Facing, turning, profiling, grooving:** X is a diameter, feeds are G95 per revolution, arcs are `G2/G3 X Z I K`.
- **Threading:** `G33 Z.. K<lead>`, with one G33 per pass (half-turns merged so the spindle-index sync starts once per pass); no G32. Optionally a one-block **`G76 P Z I J K R Q H`** cycle, chosen with the threading picker on the Post page.
- **Drilling on centre:** plain G0/G1 on X0, plus `G4 P<s>` for a floor dwell. PathPilot's lathe has no drilling cycles.
- **After each op and at the end:** `M1`/`M0`/`G30`; the program ends `M9 M5 G30 M30`.
- **Refused by name:**
  - tapping, back-boring, holes off the axis;
  - G76 records the cycle can't state exactly (compound angle, finish allowance, pull-out, unequal rungs, internal thread, or one cut from −X);
  - tool numbers outside 1-99;
  - nose-radius compensation;
  - milling work;
  - feeds with no speed;
  - C-axis sections.
- **Registration:** added to `BUILTINS` and `LATHE_POSTS`. The default lathe post is still Fanuc Lathe.
- **Not handled yet:** the threading stack's infeed and repeat-pass features (#516-#518) aren't on main. Each will need its own mapping or refusal when it lands.

## How tested
- **New `lathe_post_tormach` (9):**
  - goldens for turning, G33 threading, G76 threading and an axial drill, each in mm and inch, run through both the in-app gate and the raw stream;
  - a dwell;
  - G96 with D;
  - an arc;
  - part load;
  - a trip home;
  - the dialect refusals and the G76 refusals;
  - the registry.
- **LinuxCNC syntax check on every program:** G7 before motion, no nested comments, only documented G/M words, and no G32, G80, G81, G83, M6, G43, Y, O or `%`.
- **Conformance:** it now requires the new post to refuse every mill golden by name.
- **Gate:** golden_cl, posting, every lathe_post* and turning_* suite, machine_library, after_op, the coolant suites, tormach_post and camcraft-post all pass. Clippy is clean.

## Not exercised (draft until the Hub run)
- **Hub run:** a turning and a threading program in PathPilot Hub's 8L or 15L simulator (the issue's Done means). The machines are #611 / PR #624.
- **Assumptions to confirm on the control:**
  - G30 before each tool change (no G53 retract);
  - I/K arcs;
  - one G33 per pass;
  - the G76 I sign for tools touched off at +X.

## Update (24945aec): on top of the lathe fixes
This PR now carries **#639** (#629, thread hand), **#640** (#630, control point), **#644** (#641, blade corner) and **#648** (#632, facing approach) through merges. Review only `24945aec` beyond them.
- **Thread hand:**
  - declares `threadHands`, and writes M3, or M4 (with an operator note) on `SpindleDirection reverse`;
  - checks every G33 half-turn's arc sense against the spindle and refuses a mismatch by name;
  - G76 refuses a hand or direction that doesn't fit the spindle;
  - threads run from the start Z toward the chuck.
- **Control point:** the app sends the tool's control point, and the note states `ORIENTATION n`. The goldens shift by X−1.6 / Z−0.8 for an r0.8 orientation-2 insert.
- **G33 K:** one K per thread (the record's lead, to 6 decimals). Half-turns merge within 2.5 µm, and a stray lead is refused. A 12 TPI thread drops from 15 blocks to 3.
- **G76 rounding:** diameters agree within 2.5 µm. I, J and K are whole control steps, the root is rounded outward (never deeper than the minor), and the drive X comes from the same steps.
- **G76 words:** PathPilot's order is `P Z I J K R Q H`.
  - There is **no D**: LinuxCNC's G76 reference and Tormach's 8L page define none for G76.
  - **R1 Q0** stays as the record states, so the control cuts the equal-depth radial passes the simulation showed. R2 or Q30 waits for the infeed work (#516-#518).
- **Tests:** the suite is split into `lathe_post_tormach` (6) and `lathe_post_tormach_thread` (7, of which 4 are new):
  - LH under M4;
  - a refusal against the spindle;
  - one K per thread at 12 TPI;
  - G76 grid rounding that never goes deeper than the minor.
- **Gate:** green, including the lathe, turning and posting suites. Clippy is clean.
- **The Hub run should check:**
  1. G76 without D is accepted and cuts 3 passes Z14→Z8 under M3;
  2. LH under M4;
  3. G33 passes land in the same groove, including 12 TPI;
  4. the I/J/K sign on the 8L/15L tool post;
  5. an r0.8 insert touched off as orientation 2 finishes Ø7 at the Z2 shoulder.

Changelog: New Tormach PathPilot Lathe post (LinuxCNC G7/G18/G95, T0101, G33 passes or one-block G76 threading, drilling on centre as plain moves); selectable for lathes, with refusals by name for what PathPilot cannot run (#612)

